# Commits that moved lines without changing them. `git blame` skips these so it
# keeps pointing at whoever wrote the code, not at whoever reformatted it.
#
# GitHub reads this file automatically in its blame view. Locally it is opt-in,
# once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Add a commit here only when it is genuinely whitespace-only. A commit that
# also changed behaviour must never be listed — blame would then skip real work.

# style(tests): reindent tests/ to tabs, and enforce it (#1005)
# 250 test files, four spaces -> tabs. Verified reversible: re-expanding the
# tabs reproduced every original file byte for byte.
#
# The squash also carried four non-whitespace files (CHANGELOG.md, CLAUDE.md,
# .github/workflows/phpcs.yml, phpcs-tests.xml.dist). Ignoring a commit is
# all-or-nothing, so blame on those four skips this commit too — accepted, as
# the alternative is losing authorship across the whole test suite.
